<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/tim-cook/">Tim Cook</a> will step down as Apple's CEO on Tuesday, September 1, and ahead of that date, Apple hosted a farewell party for him. According to <em><a href="https://www.theinformation.com/articles/apple-ceos-farewell-tributes-unusually-personal-tim-cook">The Information</a></em>, the party took place on August 23, just a day before Cook <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/24/tim-cook-replaced-steve-jobs-15-years-ago-today/">celebrated his 15th anniversary</a> as Apple CEO.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/06/tim-cook-wwdc-2026.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="895" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1051289" /><br/>
Approximately 200 people celebrated Cook at the Caffé Macs cafeteria on the Apple campus, and band OneRepublic performed. Several speakers shared tributes to Cook, including Steve Jobs' wife Laurene Powell Jobs, former Apple COO Jeff Williams, Apple services chief <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/eddy-cue/">Eddy Cue</a>, and incoming CEO John Ternus.<br/>
